<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baba Ishaq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1240">1240</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baba Ishaq was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> preacher in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and disciple of the mystic Baba Ilyas. In 1239–1240 he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babai-revolt">Babai revolt</a>, a large rising of Turkmen against the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykhusraw-ii">Kaykhusraw II</a>, spreading from the south-east towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amasya">Amasya</a>. The rebels were defeated with the help of the sultan's Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, and Baba Ishaq was captured and executed.</p></div>
